use a Panel title is fixed; the stages after the first are shown by a Variant; the roots, Widget ids, counts, digests and the codes under Details are sample content.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except names, identities and the English sentences of the server under Details; en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member pressed Export handoff… on the Overview, or in the Handoff facet of the Readiness panel of a View, which starts with that View as the only root.","The base state is the whole Workspace for a holder of handoff.export: the assessment says \"Not implementation-ready\" with three blocking issues and one advisory note.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the dialog is centered over a dimmed ground and never wider than the viewport."],"intent":"Show the Export handoff dialog as built from Adapter Widgets only: choosing the roots of a bundle (the whole Workspace, or chosen Views, UX Flows and Assets), the readiness assessment of exactly those roots with its blocking and advisory sentences, and the snapshot that is exported.","interactionRules":["The assessment runs for exactly the chosen roots and again whenever they change or Recheck is pressed: a bundle holds the closure of its roots, and problems outside it never affect its readiness.","The assessment reads \"implementation-ready\" only when every View of the closure has a fresh complete formal capture, no Review thread of the closure (every Workspace thread included) is open or ready for review, and nothing else blocks; otherwise it lists each blocking issue as one sentence naming the View, the Widget a Review is anchored to, and notes each won't-do Review as advisory.","A bundle may be exported for a scope that is incomplete or not ready: Export snapshot then produces a diagnostic snapshot that claims no readiness, and only a read